WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:03.433
The agents run inside
limits they can't raise,

00:00:03.433 --> 00:00:05.933
so this week you put them to work.

00:00:05.933 --> 00:00:09.000
A first real result
takes days, not quarters,

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.267
and nothing on the
scoreboard is ticked by hand.

00:00:12.333 --> 00:00:18.767
By the end you'll know the eight
milestones, one checkpoint for each day,

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:21.667
and exactly how to earn each one.

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:24.300
Teams drift through setup for a quarter

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.867
without knowing how far along they are.

00:00:26.867 --> 00:00:31.667
Mia thinks she's nearly done, and
the scoreboard says three of eight.

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:36.400
So the week has one rule: one checkpoint
a day, scored from real facts,

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.800
never ticked by hand. The
scoreboard is the first win card,

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.333
on your organization home and on the
Setup page. It has eight milestones,

00:00:44.333 --> 00:00:48.867
and each is computed from real facts
every time you look, as done, pending,

00:00:48.867 --> 00:00:50.300
or could not read.

00:00:50.333 --> 00:00:53.867
Unknown always shows its reason
and never counts as done,

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:57.100
while pending ones carry
the exact next step.

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:59.067
Ask your agent: "What is
my next first win step".

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:02.000
It's a read, so any agent
with read access can answer.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.067
Pro move: ask it every morning,
and it becomes your standup.

00:01:06.133 --> 00:01:07.667
Day one holds two milestones.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:11.800
First, your instance is ready, which
means every required item is live,

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.900
and a model key and an email
sender are the usual ones.

00:01:14.900 --> 00:01:17.667
In the console: Setup, then
finish the required items.

00:01:17.667 --> 00:01:21.800
Or ask your agent: "What is missing
before my instance is ready,

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.367
and how much of my source is covered".

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:26.900
Second, connect your first real
data source, usually your CRM,

00:01:26.900 --> 00:01:28.900
the way Connections and
integrations showed.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:33.100
A model key or a sender key doesn't
count, and sample data never does.

00:01:33.100 --> 00:01:36.800
Then check coverage in the console,
under Connections, then Data health.

00:01:36.800 --> 00:01:40.533
You see how much of each object GTM
OS holds, and where the gaps are.

00:01:40.533 --> 00:01:42.433
Until a real source is syncing,

00:01:42.433 --> 00:01:45.233
the rest of the week has
nothing to work from.

00:01:45.300 --> 00:01:47.733
Day two, milestone three:
your first sync finished.

00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:51.033
In the console: Connections,
then Sync now on your CRM,

00:01:51.033 --> 00:01:52.167
and wait for it to complete.

00:01:52.167 --> 00:01:55.100
Or ask your agent: "Sync
HubSpot and show completeness".

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:57.567
When the records arrive and the gaps show,

00:01:57.567 --> 00:02:00.000
the numbers start to mean something.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:03.767
If the sync fails, the Connections row
shows the reason from the last check,

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:06.000
so you fix the cause instead of guessing.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:08.533
Leo owns this day, because
it's mostly keys and access.

00:02:08.567 --> 00:02:11.900
Day three, milestone four: a
person signs your first definition.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:14.600
In the console: Setup,
then Your definitions.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:17.300
Review the drafted cards,
each with its evidence.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.633
Edit what's wrong, then propose.

00:02:19.633 --> 00:02:22.033
A different person signs,
and if an agent drafted it,

00:02:22.033 --> 00:02:26.200
the person behind that agent's key
can't be the signer. Or ask your agent:

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:29.433
"Which definitions are drafted
and waiting for a signature".

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:31.300
Here's what the two people did.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:36.133
Mia reviewed the cards, fixed a
wrong segment, and proposed them.

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:39.700
Orbit helped with the drafts,
but proposing isn't signing,

00:02:39.700 --> 00:02:43.933
so Sophia read the evidence and
signed. The record shows both.

00:02:43.967 --> 00:02:47.033
Day four, milestone five:
your first Dry Mode draft.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:50.167
In the console: Settings,
then Safety, with Dry Mode on,

00:02:50.167 --> 00:02:51.600
then run one engine once.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.067
It drafts what it would
have done and sends nothing.

00:02:55.067 --> 00:02:59.467
Or ask your agent: "Run scoring once
under Dry Mode and show me the draft".

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:02.500
Now you can judge the logic
before anything leaves.

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:05.300
Day five, milestone six: your
accounts have fit scores.

00:03:05.300 --> 00:03:08.833
This needs the ICP and scoring
definitions you signed on day three.

00:03:08.833 --> 00:03:10.267
In the console: Engines, Score,

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:13.933
then score your accounts and read
the evidence behind each verdict.

00:03:13.933 --> 00:03:17.267
Or ask your agent: "Score my
accounts and explain the top three".

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:21.367
If the ranking looks wrong, tune the
scoring model instead of trusting it.

00:03:21.367 --> 00:03:23.700
The change goes through the
same propose and sign steps.

00:03:23.733 --> 00:03:27.433
Day six, milestone seven: a second
person approves a proposed action.

00:03:27.433 --> 00:03:31.500
In the console: Approvals, as the
approver, and decide the first proposal.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:36.033
The proposer can't approve it, and
neither can the human an agent acts for.

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:38.633
Or ask your agent: "What
is waiting for approval".

00:03:38.633 --> 00:03:41.533
It reports the approval
number and stops there.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:44.167
Day seven, milestone eight:
your first live message.

00:03:44.167 --> 00:03:47.300
When the Dry Mode drafts look right,
open Safety and check the engines card,

00:03:47.300 --> 00:03:49.600
so every other engine is set to Dry.

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:52.600
Turn the organization switch
off, set only Outreach to Live,

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:53.867
and approve the first send.

00:03:53.867 --> 00:03:56.733
A first message to someone nobody has
written to always waits for a person,

00:03:56.733 --> 00:03:58.700
whatever the autonomy setting.

00:03:58.700 --> 00:04:00.700
One habit worth copying:
run the go live check first.

00:04:00.700 --> 00:04:03.600
Ask your agent: "Run the go
live check", which is read only.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.900
Going live properly has its
own clip: Tutorial, going live.

00:04:06.933 --> 00:04:09.533
If a week is tight, nothing breaks,

00:04:09.533 --> 00:04:14.900
because the checklist keeps
the order and not a deadline.

00:04:14.900 --> 00:04:17.200
Two weeks is a normal pace.

00:04:17.267 --> 00:04:19.833
Last, reminders. While
setup is unfinished,

00:04:19.833 --> 00:04:22.833
owners and admins see a reminder
about the next step in the app.

00:04:22.833 --> 00:04:26.433
Email is opt in: it's off until you
turn it on, comes at most once a week,

00:04:26.433 --> 00:04:28.633
and stops when setup is complete.

00:04:28.633 --> 00:04:32.233
Every mail says why you got it
and has a one click unsubscribe.

00:04:32.233 --> 00:04:35.000
In the console: Notifications,
Setup reminders by email.

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.433
Or ask your agent: "Turn on
setup reminder emails for me".

00:04:37.433 --> 00:04:40.333
It refuses, because that's
a human only setting.

00:04:40.367 --> 00:04:45.533
Someone on your team will say: a week
is too fast for a real go to market.

00:04:45.533 --> 00:04:47.600
It's the first message,
not the whole motion.

00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:51.000
Day seven is one engine
live and one approved send,

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:54.433
with caps on and everything
else still in Dry Mode.

00:04:54.500 --> 00:04:58.500
Say it back: Eight milestones,
one checkpoint a day,

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:04.433
each scored from real facts. The last
one is a message a person approved.

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:09.500
You now have a week you can run, and
a scoreboard that can't be faked.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:14.433
Up next, bring your data in,
your whole book in one afternoon.
